window.DM_HUB={"top": "<div class=\"confidential\"><div class=\"wrap\"><b>Confidential.</b> Licensed to Dunns Food &amp; Drinks for internal sales, buying, marketing and strategic use under the partnership terms. Not to be republished, resold, embedded or shared outside Dunns without Dream Menu's written consent. <a href=\"/logout\">Sign out</a></div></div>\n<section class=\"ph-sec\" id=\"p-quarter\"><div class=\"wrap\">\n  <div class=\"ph-head\"><h2 data-short=\"This quarter\">This quarter, for partners</h2><p>Written from the data to 10 November 2026. Only moves that pass a significance test are listed.</p></div>\n  <div class=\"ph-q\">\n    <div class=\"ph-tile up\"><h3>Rising clearly <small>11</small></h3><ul><li><b>Spirits</b> <span>alcoholic drink</span><em>+8.8 pts</em></li><li><b>Whisky</b> <span>alcoholic drink</span><em>+6.6 pts</em></li><li><b>Vegetables and salad</b> <span>side</span><em>+5.6 pts</em></li><li><b>Beer and cider</b> <span>alcoholic drink</span><em>+5.4 pts</em></li></ul></div>\n    <div class=\"ph-tile dn\"><h3>Falling clearly <small>10</small></h3><ul><li><b>Cocktails</b> <span>alcoholic drink</span><em>−18.2 pts</em></li><li><b>Potatoes and fries</b> <span>side</span><em>−11.4 pts</em></li><li><b>Chicken</b> <span>starter</span><em>−4.7 pts</em></li><li><b>Skinny fries</b> <span>side</span><em>−4.7 pts</em></li></ul></div>\n    <div class=\"ph-tile\"><h3>Top scores to back</h3><ul><li><b>Whisky</b> <span>alcoholic drink</span><em>8.6/10</em></li><li><b>Lager</b> <span>alcoholic drink</span><em>7.7/10</em></li><li><b>Greens and creamed spinach</b> <span>side</span><em>7.5/10</em></li></ul></div>\n    <div class=\"ph-tile\"><h3>How operators feel</h3><ul><li><b>Confidence, next 12 months</b><em>6.2/10</em></li>\n      <li><b>See supplier prices rising</b><em>89%</em></li>\n      <li><b>Biggest pressure</b><em>energy</em></li></ul></div>\n  </div>\n  <p class=\"ph-actions\"><a class=\"cta\" href=\"/briefing\">Open the printable briefing</a> <a class=\"ph-ghost\" href=\"/onepager\">Print the one-pager for a sales meeting</a> <a class=\"ph-ghost\" href=\"#data\">Download the data</a></p>\n</div></section>\n", "bottom": "<section class=\"ph-sec ph-alt\" id=\"data\"><div class=\"wrap\"><div class=\"ph-head\"><h2>Data downloads</h2><p>CSV files for Excel or any data tool, built from the live data each time you download: interviews to 10 November 2026. Aggregated and anonymised: no names, contact details or quotes from individual guests.</p></div><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>What it holds</th><th class=\"num\">Rows</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"/partner/data/venues.csv\" data-csv=\"venues\"><b>Venues</b></a><small>venues.csv</small></td><td>Every venue guests have named: location and geocoding, mentions, guests, mentions by course, top dishes (plain labels), dishes named, address and guide awards.</td><td class=\"num\">1,935</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"/partner/data/market_categories.csv\" data-csv=\"market\"><b>Dishes by market</b></a><small>market_categories.csv</small></td><td>Leading dishes for every world, region, country, nation and city market, with the original category, a plain label and the parent group, plus counts and shares.</td><td class=\"num\">408</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"/partner/data/category_trends.csv\" data-csv=\"trends\"><b>Trends by quarter</b></a><small>category_trends.csv</small></td><td>Each course quarter by quarter at two levels, parent group and dish, with the earlier and recent pooled shares, the move, the test result and a flag for quarters with fewer than 100 answers.</td><td class=\"num\">786</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"/partner/data/course_categories.csv\" data-csv=\"course\"><b>Dishes by course</b></a><small>course_categories.csv</small></td><td>All interviews to date: parent groups and the leading dishes for each course, with soft and alcoholic drinks shown separately.</td><td class=\"num\">107</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"/partner/data/market_activity_by_quarter.csv\" download><b>Market activity by quarter</b></a><small>market_activity_by_quarter.csv</small></td><td>Venue mentions per market per quarter: which cities and neighbourhoods are gaining momentum.</td><td class=\"num\">318</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"note\">Shares exclude answers coded as Other. Locations: \"address confirmed\" is a verified address or postcode; \"approximate\" is placed on the right street, neighbourhood or town; \"not yet pinned\" is counted in its city or country.</p></div></section>\n<section class=\"ph-sec\" id=\"term\"><div class=\"wrap ph-term\"><div><div class=\"ph-head\"><h2>Your partnership this term</h2><p>1 October 2026 to 31 March 2027. What has happened and what is due next.</p></div><ol class=\"ph-time\"><li class=\"done\"><span class=\"ph-when\">1 October 2026</span><b>Partnership started</b><span>Partner briefing, map trend lines and data downloads opened.</span></li><li class=\"now\"><span class=\"ph-when\">Today</span><b>Now: Q4 2026 fieldwork</b><span>Interviews to 10 November 2026 are already in every page. The site refreshes every Monday.</span></li><li class=\"next\"><span class=\"ph-when\">After 31 December 2026</span><b>Q4 2026 review and presentation</b><span>The written Quarterly Industry Insight Review and a presentation to management and sales teams, after the quarter closes.</span></li><li class=\"next\"><span class=\"ph-when\">By 14 January 2027</span><b>Questions for Q1 2027</b><span>Send up to two commissioned questions from any department. Without them, Dream Menu sets the scope from the previous quarter.</span></li><li class=\"next\"><span class=\"ph-when\">31 March 2027</span><b>Initial term ends</b><span>The review of the final quarter follows. Reviews already delivered can be kept for internal reference.</span></li></ol></div><aside class=\"ph-ask\"><h3>Ask the panel a question</h3><p>Up to two questions a quarter, placed into live interviews and reported in the next review.</p><a class=\"cta\" href=\"mailto:contact.dreammenu@gmail.com?subject=Dunns%20commissioned%20questions&amp;body=Question%201:%0D%0A%0D%0AWhich%20department%20is%20asking:%0D%0A%0D%0AQuestion%202:%0D%0A%0D%0AWhich%20department%20is%20asking:%0D%0A\">Send your questions</a><p class=\"ph-small\">Or a new themed round, or an extra cut of the data: Gordon Best, <a href=\"mailto:contact.dreammenu@gmail.com\">contact.dreammenu@gmail.com</a>.</p></aside></div></section>\n<section class=\"ph-sec\" id=\"terms\"><div class=\"wrap\"><details class=\"ph-fold\"><summary>Terms of use and sponsorship</summary><div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"card\"><h3>Terms of use</h3><!--terms--><ul class=\"plain\">\n    <li>For Dunns' own internal sales, buying, marketing and strategic use only. The licence is non-exclusive and non-transferable.</li>\n    <li>The quarterly reviews, data extracts and map data are confidential. Do not redistribute or publish them outside Dunns without Dream Menu's written consent.</li>\n    <li>Map access is for named Dunns users and does not include any right to republish, resell or embed the platform or its rankings.</li>\n    <li>Dunns may mention the partnership in its own marketing but may not reproduce review content externally without consent.</li>\n    <li>Data is aggregated and anonymised. Dream Menu may withhold or redact material that participants have not consented to share.</li>\n    <li>The insight comes from qualitative fieldwork, given in good faith. It is not a complete or statistically representative picture of the market.</li>\n    <li>Access to the map and partner area ends if the partnership ends. Reviews already delivered can be kept for internal reference.</li></ul>\n    <p class=\"note\">Summary only. The signed partnership terms govern.</p><!--/terms--></div><div class=\"card\"><h3>Sponsorship on Dream Menu output</h3><!--spon--><ul class=\"plain\">\n    <li><b>Quarterly report:</b> cover and title-page sponsor branding. On this site, the report web edition carries the partnership line.</li>\n    <li><b>Sponsor page:</b> About Dunns and the editorial independence statement, on the <a href=\"/report#sponsor\">report overview</a>.</li>\n    <li><b>Popular Venue stickers:</b> window decals with Dunns branding, shown on <a href=\"/for-business\">For business</a>.</li>\n    <li><b>Social promotion and interview cards:</b> one sponsored post a month and a sponsor mark on every published interview card, on Instagram.</li></ul>\n    <p class=\"note\">Dream Menu keeps full editorial control. Dunns approves only the artwork and copy of its own branded elements.</p><!--/spon--></div></div></details></div></section>\n"};
